{
  "_about": "Every input action, one entry each. Controls (scripts/core/controls.gd) builds Godot's InputMap from this at start and again when the scheme changes or a binding is rebound (rebinds are saved per scheme in user://bindings.cfg). Each action has bindings per scheme: \"standard\", \"hardcore\" (the hidden Steel Battalion / QWOP layout from the physics supplement, point 6) or \"all\" (every scheme). Binding strings: key:<Godot key name> (physical key, so it follows the key's place, not its letter), mouse:left|right|middle|wheel_up|wheel_down|back|forward, joy:<button> (cross circle square triangle l1 r1 l3 r3 options create ps touchpad dpad_up dpad_down dpad_left dpad_right), joy:<axis><sign> (left_x- left_x+ left_y- left_y+ right_x- right_x+ right_y- right_y+) and joy:l2 / joy:r2 for the analog triggers. \"context\" says where an action is live (field = driving, handler = the Handler command view, ui = menus, global = everywhere); rebinding warns about clashes only inside the same scheme and a shared context. \"sticks\" pairs actions into two-axis sticks that get radial dead zones and response curves (settings controls.<settings>_inner/_outer/_curve); \"triggers\" get the trigger dead zone and curve.",
  "schemes": {
    "standard": {"label": "Standard", "hidden": false},
    "hardcore": {"label": "Hardcore manual walking", "hidden": true, "unlock_setting": "controls.hardcore_mode"}
  },
  "sticks": {
    "move": {"x": ["strafe_left", "strafe_right"], "y": ["move_back", "move_forward"], "settings": "move"},
    "aim": {"x": ["turn_left", "turn_right"], "y": ["aim_down", "aim_up"], "settings": "aim"},
    "swing": {"x": ["swing_left", "swing_right"], "y": ["swing_back", "swing_forward"], "settings": "move"},
    "com": {"x": ["com_left", "com_right"], "y": ["com_back", "com_forward"], "settings": "aim"}
  },
  "triggers": {
    "brake": "trigger",
    "fire_main": "trigger",
    "leg_lift_rl": "trigger",
